Built it following Telegram's host-control rules (from the aura-uiux Mini App reference): navigation goes through `BackButton`, Pay goes through `MainButton` (not a page-drawn footer), colors come from `--tg-theme-*`, layout respects safe-area insets and `viewportStableHeight`, closing confirmation is toggled while the address form is dirty, and haptics fire on submit/success/error. A plain-browser fallback (back link + footer Pay button) only renders when `window.Telegram.WebApp` is absent, so nothing duplicates the host UI inside Telegram.

